ifier":"s:7Afluent20RetryByCountStrategyC","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/RetryByCountStrategy","text":"RetryByCountStrategy"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SQ","text":"Equatable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","text":"Error"}]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The maximum number of times to retry the upstream, defaulting to 1.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"retries"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The specific error that should trigger a retry."}]}],"name":"error"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" that emits the same output as the upstream but retries on the specified error up to the specified number of times."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method returns an "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that retries the upstream only when the specified error occurs, up to the given number of retries."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not all "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":"s can be retried. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncThrowingStream"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be retried on their own."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Example","type":"heading","anchor":"Example"},{"code":["actor CallCounter {","    private(set) var count = 0","    func increment() -> Int {","        count += 1","        return count","    }","}","","enum CustomError: Error, Equatable {","    case temporaryFailure","}","","let counter = CallCounter()","","let sequence = DeferredTask {","    let attempt = await counter.increment()","    if attempt < 2 {","        throw CustomError.temporaryFailure","    } else if attempt == 2 {","        throw NSError(domain: \"OtherError\", code: 1, userInfo: nil)","    }","    return 7","}",".toAsyncSequence()",".retry(3, on: CustomError.temporaryFailure)","","for try await value in sequence {","    print(value) \/\/ prints 7 after retry","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not every ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can be retried, for this to work the sequence has to implement an iterator that doesn’t preserve state across various creations.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncThrowingStream"},{"text":" are notable sequences which cannot be retried on their own.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/RetryOn":{"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/retryon","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RetryOn"}],"abstract":[],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RetryOn"}],"title":"AsyncSequences.RetryOn","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryOn","role":"symbol"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncBroadcastSequence/retry(_:on:)-29m2p":{"